{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_numerical_claim_audit", "label": "Numerical-claim audit \u2014 methodology.tex and results.tex", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "340 claims traced by six parallel extractors against brain/log/*.md and the code; every fix column is a proposal and nothing was corrected or pushed."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_verdict_vocabulary", "label": "Verdict vocabulary \u2014 MATCHES / STALE / MISMATCH / UNTRACEABLE", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "STALE was expected to be the dominant defect class because the project ran successive correction passes; it turned out absent from both chapters."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_fifth_of_nine", "label": "MISMATCH 1 \u2014 'fifth of nine' is second of nine", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Report 43's own prose contradicts its own table and the chapter inherited the prose error; 'fifth' dramatises a 0.045 gap into a collapse. Fix report 43 as well, or the error will be re-inherited."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_reject_vs_demote", "label": "MISMATCH 2 \u2014 'reject' is demote", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At 273 origins rung1_robust_dow sits in the 90% set at p = 0.11; 'reject' is a term of art and this is the chapter's own closing synthesis, so the misuse is costly."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_ellel_flip_cause", "label": "MISMATCH 3 \u2014 the Ellel flip is attributed to the wrong cause", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Store growth, not fold count, unseats robust_dow; as written the chapter offers the wrong mechanism for its own central small-sample argument."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_na_cell_that_scored", "label": "MISMATCH 4 \u2014 an 'n/a' cell for a rung that scored", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An n/a in a results table asserts that a measurement was not obtained."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_untraceable_forty_pounds", "label": "UNTRACEABLE \u2014 the 'roughly \u00a340' grouped forecast", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No \u00a340 figure exists in report 47 and the nearest, \u00a344.8, is a different quantity the chapter already cites correctly two sections later; the real grouped-vs-univariate difference computed from the committed per-origin MAE vectors is \u00a34.27-\u00a310.94."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_sba_selection_direction_defect", "label": "select_sba implements the inequality reversed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The chapter's claim is correct and the code is wrong, so the chapter's SBA result has no repo artefact backing it \u2014 either fix the code and re-run, or the claim is unevidenced."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_statistical_reporting_failures", "label": "The repo computed the uncertainty and the chapter printed the point estimate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The failures are uniform in kind and the remedy is almost entirely transcription; nearly every missing interval already exists in a committed result file."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_high_tracing_rate", "label": "309 of 340 numbers resolve to a committed artefact or code constant", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The pre-registration-by-commit discipline is doing what it was meant to do; the defects are concentrated in prose about the numbers, not in the numbers."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_audit_missed_per_script_artefacts", "label": "The audit searched only brain/log and the code", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It missed ~30 per-script result artefacts sitting beside the code. Those are the primary artefacts; the log/NN_*.md reports are narrative syntheses over them and lose on disagreement."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_addendum_tab_exchangeability", "label": "ADDENDUM \u2014 tab:exchangeability audited", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never audited before because it postdates batches A-F; entering the figure programme as a known unknown is not the same as a pass. One reporting instruction: the two false-open limbs differ in n by a factor of ~50 and must not be presented as a matched pair."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_addendum_tab_vuspr", "label": "ADDENDUM \u2014 tab:vuspr audited", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_venv_is_part_of_artefact_identity", "label": "The venv is part of an artefact's identity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Running the right script in the wrong one silently replaced the entire seven-cell VUS-PR table with 'not computed, dependency unavailable' while every other number was unaffected, so a diff skimming the totals would have passed it."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_addendum_functional_pair_frame", "label": "ADDENDUM \u2014 functional_pair frame correction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "eval/functional_pair.py scored Ellel on the untrimmed 392-row frame where every other L1 package uses the trimmed 386-row frame; diagnosed as a defect rather than a design choice because the module's own comment states origin counts it did not produce. Only Ellel moves and only Ellel could."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_addendum_winkler_numerics_regime", "label": "ADDENDUM \u2014 tab:winkler's 90% set column is regime-sensitive", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Coverage and Winkler point estimates are resolution-stable; the confidence set built on them is not. An MCS is an elimination procedure over bootstrap p-values, so a perturbation too small to move a point estimate can still cross alpha and delete a set member."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_addendum_beer_hall_marginal_verdicts", "label": "ADDENDUM \u2014 Beer Hall P-A and S-A are marginal verdicts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The verdict rests on the last few per cent of its own interval; the defensible phrasing is directionally consistent but not robust, which is the same conclusion the empty adoption list reaches."}], "edges": [{"source": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_numerical_claim_audit", "target": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_verdict_vocabulary", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_numerical_claim_audit", "target": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_fifth_of_nine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_numerical_claim_audit", "target": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_reject_vs_demote", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_numerical_claim_audit", "target": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_ellel_flip_cause", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_audit.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_numerical_claim_audit", "target": "brain_ledger_numbers_audit_mismatch_na_cell_that_scored", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/ledger/numbers_